===Etymology 2===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=irr|りん|k1=りゅう|ごん|k2=ごう}}

{{IPAchar|/rimʉɡomʉ/}} → {{IPAchar|/riũɡoũ/}} → {{IPAchar|/rʲuːɡoː/}}

A variant shift from {{der|ja|ltc|-}} {{ltc-l|林檎}}. The shift in reading was due to an [[orthographic]] [[inconsistency]] in spelling the nasalized [[mora]] marked as {{ja-r|ん}} in modern Japanese.<ref name="KDJ"/> In ancient texts, this kana did not yet exist, and the sound was often spelled using the {{ja-r|む}} kana, which in certain terms shifted to, and may have been spelled as, {{ja-r|う}}.

Appears in the {{m|ja|和名類聚抄|tr=Wamyō Ruijushō}} of {{circa2|938 {{CE}}|short=1}}.<ref name="KDJ"/>

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|りゅうごう}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|りゅうごう|hhira=りうごう}}

# {{defdate|938–???}} {{lb|ja|sort=りゆうごう|rare|obsolete}} an [[apple]]

